From 39482025d5b2365e0532676f9926ea0539cb3a83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Orbit Dev <dev@orbit.invalid>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:39:58 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 17/31] fix(orbit): confirm window activation, user-context
 logoff, absolute tool paths

Activate and power decisions move to win_actions.cpp over a thin Win32Ops seam (fakes in tests).
Activate now only accepts visible top-level windows not owned by the host (else not_found) and, after
SetForegroundWindow returns TRUE, polls GetAncestor(GetForegroundWindow(), GA_ROOT) for up to 300 ms
in 20 ms steps; if the target never becomes the foreground (e.g. a full-screen game keeps it) it answers
denied and logs it. Logoff as SYSTEM runs <system32>\shutdown.exe /l in the user's session instead of the
forced WTSLogoffSession, so apps can still veto. explorer.exe, rundll32.exe and shutdown.exe are started
by absolute path (GetSystemWindowsDirectoryW / GetSystemDirectoryW).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
